  "agentSummary": "I recorded the main APIs and have one thing left to check: whether the Supabase database calls in `queries.ts` and the Supabase client in `app/account` are used anywhere I missed.\n\nInventory is recorded. Summary:\n\n- **Stripe, SDK** (`stripe` 14.25.0): the shared client is in `utils/stripe/config.ts`. It is created with `apiVersion: null`, so no API version is pinned. It is used for:\n  - Checkout session creation.\n  - Billing portal sessions.\n  - Customer create, retrieve, list and update.\n  - Subscription retrieve.\n- **Stripe, webhook:** `POST /api/webhooks` verifies the signature with `STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET`. It handles `product.*`, `price.*`, `customer.subscription.*` and `checkout.session.completed`, and syncs the results into Supabase.\n- **Stripe.js, SDK** (`@stripe/stripe-js` 2.4.0): `loadStripe` and `redirectToCheckout` in the browser.\n- **Supabase, SDK** (`@supabase/supabase-js` 2.43.4, `@supabase/ssr` 0.1.0):\n  - Auth calls: sign in with password, OTP or OAuth, sign up, sign out, password reset, `updateUser`, `getUser` and `exchangeCodeForSession`.\n  - Data access: a service-role admin client for the `products`, `prices`, `customers`, `users` and `subscriptions` tables, plus read queries in `queries.ts`.\n\n**Gaps:**\n- I read `queries.ts` only through grep, not line by line. Its `.from()` calls are noted in one call-site entry rather than recorded individually.\n- I did not read every OAuth provider or UI component. The OAuth provider list is passed through to `signInWithOAuth` at runtime.\n- No other external hosts turned up in the sources I checked. I did not open the `scripts/` or config files individually, and the repo has no `scripts/` directory.",
